  "result": "I found the bug and wrote up the plan, but haven't changed any code yet. I'd normally submit the plan for approval with ExitPlanMode, but that tool isn't available here. So here's the summary instead.\n\n**The bug:** In `src/click/types.py:750-754`, `IntRange._clamp` returns `bound - dir` when a bound is open (meaning the bound value itself isn't allowed). The caller passes `dir` pointing into the range: `1` for the minimum and `-1` for the maximum. Subtracting it moves the value one step outside the range instead of one step inside. For example:\n- `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` with `-5` returns `-1` instead of `1`.\n- `IntRange(max=5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` with `10` returns `6` instead of `4`.\n\nClosed bounds return the bound itself, so they work correctly. That's why the existing tests don't catch this.\n\n**The fix:** Change that line to `return bound + dir`.\n\n**Tests:** Add open-bound clamping cases to the `test_range` list in `tests/test_types.py`: values below an open minimum, above an open maximum, exactly on each open bound, and a range open at both ends. They should fail before the fix and pass after. Then run `pytest tests/test_types.py` and the full suite.\n\nThe full plan is in `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\some-users-report-that-quiet-wave.md`. Should I go ahead and make the change?",
